# Solis — project context

This is a Shopify theme built for Shopify Theme Store submission.

- Scaffolded from Shopify's **Skeleton Theme**, not Dawn or Horizon (neither is Theme-Store-eligible). We follow Horizon's *architecture* only: nested theme blocks, `@theme`/`@app` block targeting, `{% stylesheet %}`/`{% javascript %}` tags.
- No UI framework (React, Vue, Svelte) renders storefront markup. Liquid is the templating layer, full stop.
- No Sass/SCSS. Native CSS with custom properties only.
- Every theme setting label must go through `locales/*.schema.json` (`t:` prefix) — never hardcode English in a schema file.
- Before generating code, check whether an equivalent section/block/snippet already exists — reuse over duplication.
- If a request conflicts with a Shopify Theme Store requirement (see /theme-store-requirements/ in the handbook), flag the conflict instead of silently complying.
- If a request is ambiguous, ask a clarifying question rather than guessing an implementation.
